From: ArchPad Project <archpad@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: make register header generation deterministic

Parser.variants is a set.  Iterating it directly makes the placement of the
generated per-chip register tables depend on Python's randomized hash seed.
The generated C data is equivalent, but the header checksum recorded in DWARF
changes and consequently changes the kernel GNU build ID.

Sort the variants before emitting them so identical inputs produce identical
headers on independent builds.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/registers/gen_header.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/registers/gen_header.py b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/registers/gen_header.py
index 798fa28c3e9c..2e257f5c3e25 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/registers/gen_header.py
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/registers/gen_header.py
@@ -760,7 +760,7 @@ class Parser(xml.parsers.expat.ParserCreate):
 						if reg == vreg:
 							d[(usage, sanitize_variant(variant))].append(reg)
 				else:
-					for variant in self.variants:
+					for variant in sorted(self.variants):
 						d[(usage, sanitize_variant(variant))].append(reg)
 
 		print("#ifdef __cplusplus")
-- 
